vely. Betting here turns your hand into a bluff; if you bet, you likely only get called by hands that beat you (a diamond or a pair). Checking allows you to realize your equity for free, keeping the pot small and giving you a chance to win at showdown if the opponent is also on a weak hand.\n\nReason: You have Ace-high on a very wet board (4-flush). The opponent has shown weakness by checking three times. Checking back is the safest play to see the river for free, as betting risks a check-raise or getting called by a superior hand while offering little value.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
